{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788269357,"nonce":"ZtYlCvT2hpKDZw3FSJi3q7rwmDQ=","message":"SCOPE SPLIT for the current round (the one that makes blueprints buildable),\nrecorded because the round's own brief left it undecided and a worker would\notherwise have to guess.\n\n\nThe brief's goal line names \"build and place-layout (3.3)\". Its DONE MEANS\nsection names only:\n\n\u003e `build {def, pos, rot, stuff}` places a blueprint the game would accept,\n\u003e refuses with the game's own sentence when it would not, and the agent can read\n\u003e back whether it stalled, progressed, or finished\n\nAnd its session split assigns `build` to **nobody** — session A is the shared\nsite routine (`8b4839f`, the `rot` argument, `c718e4a`), session B is\n\"consumers\" (`3a5ff6c`, `0d9cbd7`, blueprint observation), session C is geometry\nand touches no C#. The verb the round is named for had no owner.\n\n\n**This round ships `build`. `place-layout` / `cancel-layout` / IR consumption is\nthe next round.** Two reasons, in order of weight:\n\n1. **DONE MEANS is the contract.** This project's own rule is that the\n   Acceptance section is the definition of done (CLAUDE.md, \"Specs are\n   contracts\"). DONE MEANS names one verb and one read. The goal line is the\n   summary; where they disagree the contract wins.\n2. **`place-layout` depends on things this round is only now creating.** Module\n   phase and the \"row 0 = north\" pin are session C's output, and\n   `place-layout --origin P` cannot state its own convention until the pin\n   exists. Shipping it in the same round would mean specifying it against a\n   decision made in a parallel session.\n\n**`build` lands in session B, not a fourth session.** Comment #7 already\nestablishes that 3.3's instant mode IS `dev:spawn-thing {buildable:true}`, which\nis `3a5ff6c`'s scope and session B's work. Splitting `build` into its own\nsession means two sessions writing the same `SiteGate` call against the same\nDLL, serially, for no gain. Session B's scope is therefore: `3a5ff6c` +\n`build {def,pos,rot,stuff}` + the construction read + `0d9cbd7`.\n\n\nFiled as **`d7c8088`** — \"Nothing reads blueprints or frames: a placed build is\ninvisible, and completion is an absence\". `grep Blueprint Source/AutoRimmer/`\nreturns zero; `digest` has no construction section. Without it `build` can\nsatisfy its own acceptance and still leave the play loop unable to tell a\nmaterial stall from a finished room.\n\nThat issue also pins something this spec owes and has never stated: **this\nissue's \"every placement journaled with a placement id\" is what makes completion\nobservable at all**, because a finished build leaves no blueprint and no frame,\nso `built` and `cancelled` are otherwise the same absence. The placement id is\nnot bookkeeping — it is the only handle the completion answer can hang on.\n\n\nNothing in this issue's scope is dropped. `place-layout`'s preflight-every-cell\nrule, the `--partial` invariant, the per-cell `{at, role, reason, blocker}`\nshape and the stuff-map are all still the spec. They are next, not now — and\nthey start unblocked, because the module grid and the north pin land in this\nround.","files":null}]}